+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html lang="en">
+<head>
+  <meta charset="UTF-8">
+  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
+  <title>SCIMA Learning</title>
+  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
+  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
+  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Nunito:wght@400;500;600;700;800;900&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
+  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../app/dashboard.css">
+  <!--
+    SCIMA Learning — Library page: Library + Capture (six-page build; see the
+    landing index.html header for the map). The sources → cards pipeline in
+    one document: import/read/cite in Library, then Quick Add / AI Generate
+    in Capture, switching via the in-page tab bar (or #capture / #library).
+    Old /capture/ URLs redirect here. Manifest notes: this is the only page
+    that imports files, so it carries process-shim.js (must precede the epub
+    bundle — it polyfills the Node `process` global the bundled
+    path-resolution code expects), fflate (Library "Import" .zip and
+    exportSourceWithBookmarks), and the EPUB/MOBI parser bundles.
+    dashboard-decks.js provides the citation pickers/viewer, the chunked-blob
+    helpers and openCreateDeckModal() these flows call. pdf.min.js is still
+    lazy-loaded on demand via assetUrl(). KaTeX is NOT loaded — capture
+    previews are plain text and the reader shows source HTML as authored.
+  -->
+</head>
+<body>
+  <div id="stripe"></div>
+  <button id="nav-pill" aria-label="Open navigation menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="sidebar" title="Menu">☰</button>
